course: dictionary
lesson: 4308
title: Groan: a sound and a feeling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A groan is a long, low sound that a person makes when they are in pain, unhappy, bored or annoyed. Groan can be a verb (to groan) or a noun (a groan). «Mum groans: "No more sweets, they're bouncing off the walls on all that sugar!"» Mum is not singing. The mess and the sugar have fed her up, so groan shows she is annoyed.
explain: Look at the words around groan to find its feeling. Ask yourself what is happening and how the person feels. A groan at bad news, a bad joke or homework is a sound that says "oh no" without any words.
explain: Groan can also be used for things. A heavy old floor or a table full of food can groan, which means it makes a low creaking sound under the weight. Here groan does not mean a feeling at all, but the sound is still long and low.
fact: «Groan» can be a verb (to groan) or a noun (a groan).
fact: To groan is to make a long, low sound because you are in pain, unhappy, bored or annoyed.
fact: Heavy things can groan too, like an old floor or a table full of food.
fact: A bad pun that makes people groan is called a groaner, and the groan is part of the fun.
fact: If someone groans because they are hurt, they may need help, so tell a grown-up.
exercise: «Mum groans: "No more sweets, they're bouncing off the walls!"» What does the groan show about Mum? | She is singing a happy song | She is very hungry for cake | *She is fed up and annoyed | She is very cold
exercise: Which of these can groan, as in make a low creaking sound under weight? | A bright red balloon | A thin pencil | A cup of warm tea | *An old wooden floor
exercise: Everyone groans when Dad tells a bad joke. What does the groan tell you? | They are crying with joy | They are about to sing a song | *They think the joke is bad and are annoyed or amused | They have all fallen asleep
test: «A pun that makes everyone groan has still worked; the groan is part of the fun.» What is a groan in this sentence? | A word for a pun | A loud cheer | *A long, low sound people make at a bad joke | A kind of song
test: A friend falls off a bike and groans in pain. What should you do? | Ask them to groan again | Laugh at them | Walk away and forget about it | *Get help from a grown-up
exam: In «The groan from the back row told the teacher the homework news was not welcome», what is a groan? | A kind of food | A song | A shout of joy | *A long, low sound showing dislike
